<title>USA: Seligman launches 2 value funds.</title>
<headline>Seligman launches 2 value funds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seligman Group of Funds said it launched the Seligman Large-Cap Value Fund and the Seligman Small-Cap Value Fund.</p>
<p>Three classes of fund shares are offered to investors. Class A shares are offered at net asset value plus a sales load, Class B shares are offered at net asset value with a deferred sales load imposed upon redemption and Class D shares have no sales load if held for a minimum of one year.</p>
<p>J. &amp; W. Seligman &amp; Co Inc, an investment manager and advisor with approximately $19 billion in assets, manages the Seligman Group of Funds.</p>
</text>
